      "text": [
        "How we compare",
        "Why families choose Sensphere",
        "Two quick comparisons most parents are weighing when they get in touch.",
        "When NHS waiting lists feel too long",
        "NHS paediatric occupational therapy is free, but waiting lists for community OT often run into many months, sometimes longer. Sensphere is private and paid: we typically begin within weeks, work to goals we agree with you, and produce a written report families and schools can use straight away. Repo",
        "Sensphere is independent of NHS pathways and does not replace formal NHS clinical referrals.",
        "What you get from Sensphere",
        "Our practice is HCPC-registered, RCOT-member, and built around children with sensory, motor, and neurodevelopmental differences, including autism. Reports are properly explained so parents, teachers and SENCOs can put them to work the day they arrive."
      ]
    },
